WIRE (platform.minimax.io/docs/api-reference/text/api/openapi-chat-openai.json, fetched 2026-09-25): ChatCompletionReq.thinking = {type: enum[disabled, adaptive], default adaptive}. No 'enabled' value, no budget_tokens / budget field, no effort field. M3: disabled = answer directly, adaptive = thinking on (equal to omitting the field). M2.x: 'disabled is accepted but thinking remains on' (text-openai-api page, Thinking Control). reasoning_split is output formatting only, not a toggle. /anthropic CreateMessageReq (openapi-chat-anthropic.json, same date): same enum, default disabled, no output_config. That confirms the k209 part-2 fix.
PROVIDER'S OWN MAPPING: MiniMax /v1/responses (openapi-responses.json, same date): reasoning.effort enum [minimal, low, medium, high, none], default none. 'Set effort to a non-none value to enable Adaptive Thinking, but this does not tune M3's reasoning depth.' So MiniMax maps effort to the toggle exactly like this: none -> off, any level -> adaptive.
PROFILE CHECK: Profile has control enum 'boolean' and disable_form enum [absent, explicit_none, think_false, budget_zero]. disable_form is DESCRIPTIVE only: no serializer reads it. Reasoning::to_openai always emits reasoning_effort and cannot emit thinking:{type:disabled}. The Profile cannot express this today without a new enum value.
RECOMMEND (effort mapping, not a new boolean capability): (1) Profile rows: qr/\AMiniMax-M3(?!\d)/ with control=>'boolean', can_disable=>1, disable_form=>'thinking_disabled' (new DisableForm value). M2.x rows with control=>'boolean', can_disable=>0. (2) Engine::MiniMax: layer-3 correction that turns reasoning_effort back ON for MiniMax-M3 only (M2.x stays cleared, because nothing is controllable there). Add an engine-scoped reasoning_kwargs_for (the DeepSeek precedent) that reads the Profile: none -> thinking:{type:'disabled'} when can_disable, any other level -> thinking:{type:'adaptive'} (explicit, which mirrors MiniMax's own /v1/responses and survives a default flip), unset -> nothing. Keep the k204 supports() gate inside the override. (3) MiniMaxAnthropic can then send an explicit thinking:{type:disabled} for none from the same row. Today it omits the field, and the endpoint default is disabled, so the result is correct but implicit. (4) POD: the level ladder collapses to a binary. low and high both mean adaptive.
RISK: M3 supports() reasoning_effort, yet every level gives the same depth. Document it. Callers should not expect graded effort.

